# Story page: mirror
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Glass Hall
---
The Glass Hall is a corridor of mirrors in which a snake may walk into one wall and stumble out of another, an arrangement the architects have declined to explain.

Fleas live here, hopping from reflection to reflection and paying no rent at all, which I resent, as I pay a great deal of rent for a small room above a laundromat.

In one mirror {name}'s reflection was enormous and ancient and coiled around the whole world. It winked. {name} was busy screaming, and did not wink back.
